        "command"
      ],
      "description": "Whether the latest valid `emir verify-sim` record of this machine for the simulator, version, output format and simulator arguments that wrote the run's currents passed with this emir minor version (`verified`, EMIR-I463). `not verified` gives its `reason`: `no record` or `other host` or `stale` (a pass of another emir minor version) with EMIR-W464 and `command`, the verification to run; `failed` (the latest record failed: a later failure cancels an earlier pass) with EMIR-W414; `version unknown` (neither the result's header nor the names sidecar of `emir simulate` says the version: never matched to a record, `command` null) with EMIR-W416; `format not covered` (an output format emir verify-sim never writes, such as CSDF: no record can match, `command` null) with EMIR-W464; `records unreadable` (this user may not read the records file: no record counts and none could be kept, `command` null; EMIR-W415 and EMIR-W464). A verification covers kinds of current (`current_kinds`, one entry per kind the run read: the branch currents, `covered` by the record, `verify_sim_covers` whether a verification of this emir could): a run whose kinds are not all covered (a record made before records said what they cover) is `not verified`, `reason` `current kinds not covered`, with EMIR-W464. `sim_args` is what the result's names sidecar says the simulator was given (`sim_args_known` false: the result does not say, and it is matched as given none). `ignored_records` counts invalid records, `records_problem` says why a records file cannot be read at all (EMIR-W415)."
    },
